cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "parametric-insurance-design"
abstract: >-
  A Python library for designing parametric insurance payouts: a step payout
  on a hazard index, calibrated on simulated events by an optimisation under a
  premium budget. It carries a weighted-CVaR (tail-risk) objective, solved as a
  linear program, and the joint calibration of one owner's sites across a
  portfolio.
authors:
  - family-names: Prinzing
    given-names: Marc
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-11-02
repository-code: "https://github.com/marc272/parametric-insurance-design"
keywords:
  - parametric insurance
  - basis risk
  - CVaR
  - linear programming
  - catastrophe risk
